window.docContents[233].resolve({"/Exponential___-Logarithmic___-Sine___-and-Cosine-Integrals/___6___18-Methods-of-Computation/#LMLF-___-DLMF-with-Lean--Exponential___-Logarithmic___-Sine___-and-Cosine-Integrals--___6___18-Methods-of-Computation--___6___18-Methods-of-Computation":{"contents":"This section surveys numerical methods and records the auxiliary-function\nrecurrence in a typed, convergence-aware form. The appropriate method depends\non scale, cancellation, phase, and whether a function is evaluated by a\nconvergent series, an asymptotic expansion, quadrature, or a continued\nfraction.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n","context":"LMLF · DLMF with Lean\u0009Exponential, Logarithmic, Sine, and Cosine Integrals\u0009§6.18 Methods of Computation","header":"§6.18 Methods of Computation","id":"/Exponential___-Logarithmic___-Sine___-and-Cosine-Integrals/___6___18-Methods-of-Computation/#LMLF-___-DLMF-with-Lean--Exponential___-Logarithmic___-Sine___-and-Cosine-Integrals--___6___18-Methods-of-Computation--___6___18-Methods-of-Computation"},"/Improper-integrals/3___3-Algebra-and-a-change-of-starting-point/#LMLF-___-DLMF-with-Lean--Improper-integrals--3___3-Algebra-and-a-change-of-starting-point":{"contents":"Finite sums may be formed before integration. Each summand may also be sent through its own\ncontinuous linear map; the exceptional set of the sum is the union of the individual exceptional\nsets, and the value is the corresponding sum of mapped values.\n\n\n\nIf f is integrable on the compact prefix from a to k, moving the starting point from k back\nto a adds precisely that ordinary integral to the improper value.\n\n\n\n","context":"LMLF · DLMF with Lean\u0009Improper integrals","header":"3.3 Algebra and a change of starting point","id":"/Improper-integrals/3___3-Algebra-and-a-change-of-starting-point/#LMLF-___-DLMF-with-Lean--Improper-integrals--3___3-Algebra-and-a-change-of-starting-point"}});